  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/AGENT_BUSY" target="_blank">AGENT_BUSY</a> indicates that the "busy" <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Internal_Animations" target="_blank">internal animation</a> is playing, even if the user is not truly in busy mode.</li>
    <li><b>On server 1.40 and below</b>, <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/AGENT_TYPING" target="_blank">AGENT_TYPING</a> indicated that the "type" internal animation is playing, it would not be set if the user disabled <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Debug_Settings" target="_blank">PlayTypingAnim</a>. <b>On server 1.42 and up</b>, it reflects <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/ChatFromViewer" target="_blank">typing start/stop messages</a> from the client and does not depend on the animation. If the old behavior is desired, use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetAnimationList" target="_blank">llGetAnimationList</a> and look for "c541c47f-e0c0-058b-ad1a-d6ae3a4584d9" &#8212; <a href="https://jira.secondlife.com/browse/SVC-787" target="_blank">SVC-787</a></li>
    <li>`<a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/AGENT_ALWAYS_RUN" target="_blank">AGENT_ALWAYS_RUN</a> | <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/AGENT_WALKING" target="_blank">AGENT_WALKING</a>` indicates that the user requested to run using standard viewer controls. Use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetAnimation" target="_blank">llGetAnimation</a> to also detect running caused by physics.</li>
    <li>This function does not return reliable information immediately after a border crossing. Use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetAnimation" target="_blank">llGetAnimation</a> instead, if you can. &#8212; <a href="https://jira.secondlife.com/browse/SVC-3177" target="_blank">SVC-3177</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/AGENT_AUTOMATED" target="_blank">AGENT_AUTOMATED</a> may unexpectedly be enabled, see <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/AGENT_AUTOMATED" target="_blank">its caveats</a> for more detail.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local buf = #events
    buf = ll.GetAgentInfo(ll.DetectedKey(0))
    local out = ""
    if bit32.btest(buf, AGENT_FLYING) then
        out ..= "The agent is flying.\n"
    else
        out ..= "The agent is not flying.\n"
    end

    if bit32.btest(buf, AGENT_ATTACHMENTS) then
        if bit32.btest(buf, AGENT_SCRIPTED) then
            out ..= "The agent has scripted attachments.\n"
        else
            out ..= "The agent's attachments are unscripted.\n"
        end
    else
        out ..= "The agent does not have attachments.\n"
    end

    if bit32.btest(buf, AGENT_MOUSELOOK) then
        out ..= "the agent is in mouselook."
    else
        out ..= "the agent is in normal camera mode."
    end
    ll.Whisper(0, out)
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    touch_start(integer buf)
    {
        buf = llGetAgentInfo(llDetectedKey(0));
        string out;
        if(buf & AGENT_FLYING)
            out += "The agent is flying.\n";
        else
            out += "The agent is not flying.\n";
 
        if(buf & AGENT_ATTACHMENTS)
        {
            if(buf & AGENT_SCRIPTED)
                out += "The agent has scripted attachments.\n";
            else
                out += "The agent's attachments are unscripted.\n";
        }
        else
            out += "The agent does not have attachments.\n";
 
        if(buf & AGENT_MOUSELOOK)
            out += "the agent is in mouselook.";
        else
            out += "the agent is in normal camera mode.";
        llWhisper(0, out);
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>This is not a good way of testing if an avatar is in the region, use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetAgentSize" target="_blank">llGetAgentSize</a> instead.</p>
